<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johannes Sturm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1507–1589</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johannes Sturm was a German humanist and educator who founded the Protestant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gymnasium">Gymnasium</a> of Strasbourg in 1538 and directed it for more than 40 years. His curriculum, based on classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a>, eloquence and piety, became a model for Protestant grammar schools across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and his school was raised to an academy in 1566.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johannes-sturm.jpg" alt="Johannes Sturm" width="217" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacob van der Heyden after Tobias Stimmer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johannes_Sturm_by_Jacob_van_der_Heyden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
